(defmodule tramp
  "**Files reached another way** — Emacs's TRAMP: a file edited as root (`/sudo::`,
`M-x sudo-edit`) or on another machine that has no bedit (`/ssh:host:path`, and root on it
through `|sudo:`).

The context's details live under `src/tramp/`: editing over ssh (`tramp/ssh`), the ssh
transport — one shared connection a host, its listings kept (`tramp/ssh-transport`) — the root
hops of an ssh path (`tramp/ssh-root`), editing as root here (`tramp/sudo`), and the job every
such read and write runs as, off the loop (`tramp/job`). The path syntax itself is `sshpath`,
which the core reads.

Nothing outside calls into it: each method registers a FILE HANDLER
(`model/register-file-handler`), and opening, saving, reverting, dired, completion and
recovery go through the handler that claims a path. Loading this module registers both."
  (:use tramp/sudo :only []) ; /sudo::PATH and M-x sudo-edit, its mode-line chip
  (:use tramp/ssh :only [])) ; /ssh:host:PATH, its mode-line chip
